WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.880
In less than three decades, Helen&nbsp;
Hunt has gone from the very top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:08.160
of the film industry to, well, a lot of places.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.520
Both in and out of Hollywood, breakups&nbsp;
are a common part of adulthood. Even so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.360
Helen Hunt surprised many in 2017&nbsp;
by calling things off with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:19.960
boyfriend of 16 years, producer Matthew Carnahan.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:25.880
The two had been together since 2001, and even&nbsp;
welcomed a daughter together in 2004. And yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:30.800
despite In Touch Weekly reporting that Hunt and&nbsp;
Carnahan appeared to be crazy for each other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.800
they couldn't keep their spark alive forever.&nbsp;
According to a source who spoke to the tabloid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.080
their separation was pretty turbulent.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:42.600
That same source revealed that the pair had&nbsp;
done this several times before, recalling,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.480
"Matthew moved out a few times over the&nbsp;
years. Helen would always take him back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.320
and then time would pass and&nbsp;
she'd kick him out again."

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:54.040
Now, however, it seems they're done for real&nbsp;
and even their mutual love for their daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:58.480
Makena Lei Gordon Carnahan, couldn't&nbsp;
keep them together any longer.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:05.360
On May 13, 2004, shortly before her 41st&nbsp;
birthday, Helen Hunt gave birth to Makena.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.400
Given this was such a big change in her&nbsp;
life, it's unsurprising that Hunt pulled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:14.080
back from the Hollywood grindstone for a&nbsp;
while. After four decades without kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:19.120
it's completely understandable that Hunt wanted&nbsp;
to stay home more to raise her firstborn.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:24.240
In fact, even during her rare forays back&nbsp;
into the public eye during Makena's childhood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:30.160
her focus was still very much on her daughter.&nbsp;
She even spent the entire duration of a 2013&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:34.200
interview with The Independent knitting&nbsp;
a doll for her daughter while fielding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.640
questions about how a movie she starred&nbsp;
in would do in the upcoming award season.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.360
Now that Makena is a legal adult, we may start&nbsp;
to see more of her mother in the celebrity world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:49.400
again. However, given that Makena remains her only&nbsp;
child, we wouldn't be surprised if Hunt continued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:54.520
to dedicate massive amounts of her energy toward&nbsp;
the continued love and support of her daughter.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:58.880
Makena is already embarking on her own&nbsp;
creative endeavors as a songwriter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.600
and as a fellow artist it would only make&nbsp;
sense that Hunt would want to continue a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.650
close relationship with her daughter&nbsp;
as she transitions into adulthood.

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.720
"The two of them write the songs together&nbsp;
and they — I just hear them downstairs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:13.920
like laughing, or they'll write some sad&nbsp;
lyric and then I hear 'That's cool!'"

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.680
In the time since her heyday&nbsp;
at the turn of the century,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:21.920
Helen Hunt never outright stopped making&nbsp;
movies. However, with a few exceptions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:27.440
odds are a large portion of her long-time fans&nbsp;
may not have heard of most of those projets.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.920
At the height of her career, Hunt starred&nbsp;
in films like 1997's As Good As It Gets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.600
and the combination of her charisma&nbsp;
and chemistry with co-star Jack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:43.080
Nicholson netted the rom-com almost $315&nbsp;
million worldwide. A year before that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:48.480
she was in Twister, a disaster epic&nbsp;
that grossed almost $500 million.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:55.320
Right after her sitcom, Mad About You ended, she&nbsp;
starred in 2000's What Women Want and Cast Away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.320 --> 00:03:01.280
which took in $375 million and&nbsp;
$430 million, respectively.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.880
“I’m gonna miss the excitement&nbsp;
but I’ll handle it.”

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:07.960
Throughout the aughts, she also starred in&nbsp;
films like The Curse of the Jade Scorpion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:13.080
Dr. T &amp; the Women, and Bobby, all of which&nbsp;
failed to impress moviegoers. Critically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:19.520
her rock bottom moment has to be 2010's Every Day,&nbsp;
which opened in three theaters, never made it past&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:27.600
four, and ultimately grossed a paltry $46,029&nbsp;
over ten weeks. This film in particular was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:33.720
pretty serious disappointment, as it marked Hunt's&nbsp;
return to the screen after a three-year hiatus.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:38.560
In an interview with The Daily Beast, Helen Hunt&nbsp;
said that part of the reason she shifted into low&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:45.040
gear after her late '90s boom was due to her Oscar&nbsp;
win for As Good As It Gets. She explained that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:50.080
after making an arrangement with Sony, she&nbsp;
began writing heavily between acting gigs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:55.200
Around this time she received a copy of&nbsp;
Elinor Lipman's novel Then She Found Me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:00.880
and she began working hard to adapt it against the&nbsp;
changing tide of the film industry. Hunt recalled,

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:04.560
"I'd just been in the last big wave&nbsp;
of movies about people talking to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.160
each other and trying to love each&nbsp;
other, so as that was shrinking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.840
I was trying to make one of those&nbsp;
movies. So I kept rewriting it subtly."

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:17.400
As a result of the public's changing taste,&nbsp;
studios stopped funding the style of movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:22.680
Hunt was known for. The actress elaborated&nbsp;
that, in turn, she got pretty tired of making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:28.920
romantic comedies herself, so it was pretty apt&nbsp;
timing for a change in her creative pursuits.

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:34.600
Despite the changing time, Hunt wound up using&nbsp;
her adaption of And Then She Found Me as her first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:41.120
foray into directing and starring in a film.&nbsp;
Unfortunately, the 2007 dramedy, and Hunt's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:47.480
performance in particular, fell flat with critics.&nbsp;
One reviewer for The Los Angeles Times wrote,

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:52.080
"The problem isn’t so much the character of&nbsp;
April as it is the way Hunt plays her — a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.960
little too whiny, a little too angry to be&nbsp;
very sympathetic. Hunt has a tendency to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:00.560
play up those characteristics in&nbsp;
just about everything she does."

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.760
Hunt's debut as a director was also criticized,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:09.040
with Christy DeSmith of the Minneapolis Star&nbsp;
Tribune calling her direction "heavy-handed"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:13.320
before expanding that her acting&nbsp;
performance was also lackluster.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:19.760
After her feature-length directorial debut failed&nbsp;
critically, Hunt took a long break from directing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:24.920
Then, over the past decade, she began&nbsp;
pursuing the artform in earnest once again.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:26.480
"Any thoughts on how?"

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:28.640
Recently, she's focused mainly on television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:34.800
overseeing an episode of Californication, two&nbsp;
episodes of Revenge, two of Life In Pieces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:39.880
and one each of House of Lies, This&nbsp;
Is Us, and Feud: Bette and Joan.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:44.480
In 2014, she directed her second&nbsp;
film with Ride. While it wasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:49.480
her best creative effort to date —&nbsp;
earning only 52% on Rotten Tomatoes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:55.200
she's clearly working hard to get better at her&nbsp;
new profession and will only improve over time.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:59.320
Before Bobby and Then She Found Me,&nbsp;
critics also tore apart A Good Woman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:03.920
a film adaptation of an Oscar Wilde&nbsp;
play. Speaking to Paste Magazine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:08.960
Hunt explained that she drew great inspiration&nbsp;
from the play and its lead role, saying,

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:12.800
"It has all the earmarks of a really&nbsp;
good part. I certainly saw in there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:16.240
the potential for a character I&nbsp;
haven't seen in a little while."

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:22.080
Hunt played the seductive Mrs. Erlynne. While&nbsp;
the part in question may have been juicy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:27.200
critics didn't exactly love what Hunt did&nbsp;
with it. A review by The A.V. Club criticized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:32.280
the actor's performance as "embarrassingly&nbsp;
out of place," with many of her mannerisms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:38.520
lacking the sensual allure the role called for.&nbsp;
Another harsh review in The Seattle Times noted,

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:43.160
"[Hunt] is completely at sea here, flatly&nbsp;
intoning her lines as if she'd memorized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:48.880
them phonetically [...] It's a mystifyingly bad&nbsp;
performance, and it drags down the entire movie."

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.840
With reviews like that coming in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:55.240
we'd probably consider taking a step&nbsp;
away from the big screen as well.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:07:00.840
Even before her film career blew up, Helen Hunt&nbsp;
slowed her professional pace in the wake of Mad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:05.640
About You. One possible explanation for why&nbsp;
she did this is that she'd simply made a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:10.880
of money. With a successful show already under&nbsp;
her belt, she had little need to work unless she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:16.200
really wanted to. For this reason she could also&nbsp;
afford to be picky regarding potential roles.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:22.240
Hunt's wealth increased magnificently in May&nbsp;
1998, as she and her Mad About You co-star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:31.120
Paul Reiser negotiated pay raises from $250,000 an&nbsp;
episode to an incredible $1 million per episode.&nbsp;

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:34.600
Though this pay grade only lasted&nbsp;
them through the final season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:39.000
its 22 episodes still netted&nbsp;
both of them over 8 figures.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:44.240
Once you factor those paychecks in with the money&nbsp;
she'd made starring in Hollywood blockbusters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:50.240
you can see how acting has given her wealth beyond&nbsp;
most anyone's wildest dreams. So next time you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:56.920
wondering why Helen Hunt isn't everywhere anymore,&nbsp;
the answer might just be: she doesn't have to be.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:00.920
One of the hardest things for anyone to&nbsp;
face is the death of a family member,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:04.520
and in 2016, Hunt suffered the loss of her father.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:11.200
On December 17 of that year, Gordon Hunt, famed&nbsp;
director of cartoons and live-action television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:15.320
passed away at the age of 87. According&nbsp;
to the Hollywood Reporter, he had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:18.480
suffering from Parkinson's&nbsp;
disease prior to his death.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:22.000
Gordon Hunt had his foot in many&nbsp;
doors of the entertainment industry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.480
and even worked with some of the&nbsp;
biggest names in Hollywood today.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:28.720
"Gordon hunt was my acting teacher&nbsp;
when I was in LA for a couple years."

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:34.840
It may not surprise avid Hunt fans that Gordon&nbsp;
actually directed 31 episodes of Mad About You.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:39.480
In fact, he even directed the episode in&nbsp;
which his daughter's character gave birth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:43.920
which must have been quite a surreal&nbsp;
experience for both the actress and her father

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:47.240
Speaking to the Hollywood&nbsp;
Reporter, Hunt said of her father,

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:53.720
"If you asked 100 people who knew him, 100 of them&nbsp;
would say he was the kindest man they ever knew."

00:08:53.720 --> 00:09:00.280
Even before his death, she honored him by&nbsp;
dedicating her 2014 surfing film Ride to him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:06.480
Reportedly, Gordon was an active bodysurfer from&nbsp;
the 1930s until just a few years before his death.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:11.240
In addition to her illustrious film and TV&nbsp;
career, Hunt has also been a very public advocate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:17.240
for women's rights. In 2012, Hunt appeared on&nbsp;
NBC's Who Do You Think You Are?, a show showing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:21.960
celebrities learning about their family tree.&nbsp;
During her appearance on the show, Hunt learned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:27.040
that her great-great-grandmother was a pivotal&nbsp;
figure in the battle for women's equality.

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:32.000
This revelation must have ignited a spark in&nbsp;
Hunt, as she's been vocal about women's rights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:37.480
both in and out of Hollywood since. During&nbsp;
a 2015 interview with the Huffington Post,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:42.320
Hunt was openly critical of the limited range&nbsp;
of roles available to women of all ages.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:46.880
She criticized the industry for its lacking&nbsp;
amount of stories with strong female leads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:50.000
and how even projects as simple&nbsp;
as billboard advertisements&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:54.160
often try to sexualize models and&nbsp;
actresses for no logical reason.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:58.080
She later made her stance further known&nbsp;
by joining the Women's March to protest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:02.080
the inauguration of Donald Trump in&nbsp;
response to the derogatory things he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:07.280
said about women before and during his&nbsp;
campaign. Even if Hunt never acts again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:10.760
she's certainly got plenty of&nbsp;
work ahead of her in philanthropy.

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:16.280
In 2017, Helen Hunt was primed for a cinematic&nbsp;
comeback after being tapped for a major role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:22.880
in a new film. Written and directed by Louis C.K,&nbsp;
the black-and-white I Love You, Daddy starred C.K.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:28.160
as a TV writer who doesn't know what to do when&nbsp;
his young daughter, played by Chloe Grace Moretz,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:34.640
starts to date a significantly older and famously&nbsp;
sleazy filmmaker played by John Malkovich. Hunt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:39.760
co-starred in the film, playing the ex-wife&nbsp;
to C.K.'s character and mother of Moretz's.

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:45.440
I Love You, Daddy was set for a star-studded&nbsp;
premiere in New York on November 17, 2017,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:49.240
but the event was canceled at the last minute&nbsp;
after the New York Times' published accounts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:54.640
of five women who accused C.K. of sexual&nbsp;
misconduct. A subsequent theatrical release&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:59.889
was immediately taken off the table as well,&nbsp;
as C.K. bought back the rights to the film.

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:03.560
In November 2019, Helen Hunt&nbsp;
returned to the role of Jamie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:07.800
for the reboot of Mad About You. Her&nbsp;
time on the original show not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:12.501
made her famous, but netted her four&nbsp;
Emmy Awards and three Golden Globes.

00:11:12.501 --> 00:11:17.040
"Once we got into the space,&nbsp;
it felt wildly familiar."

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:20.240
While its initial run on NBC ended in 1999,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:24.240
it came back to TV on the tail end of&nbsp;
the reboot craze that saw other '90s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:30.200
hits like Twin Peaks, The X-Files, and&nbsp;
Roseanne return to open-armed viewers.

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:36.040
The 12 new episodes of the series focused on the&nbsp;
once-young and newlywed Jamie and Paul wondering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:41.920
what to do with themselves after their only child&nbsp;
leaves for college. Mad About You version 2.0,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:45.680
however, just didn't click as well&nbsp;
as its fellow revived classics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:50.440
earning a middling 42% rating&nbsp;
from critics on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:53.600
If fans wanted to watch it, it&nbsp;
was also kind of hard for them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:56.960
to find. The season aired on Spectrum Originals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.960 --> 00:12:02.080
a relatively obscure network that serves as&nbsp;
the showcase channel for a cable company.

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:06.000
In 2017, Helent Hunt found herself&nbsp;
at the center of an international&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:11.280
controversy. She agreed to participate in&nbsp;
an event known as the World Youth Forum,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:15.280
which took place in Sharm&nbsp;
El-Sheikh a resort city in Egypt.

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:18.720
As a high-profile celebrity, Hunt&nbsp;
was made a featured speaker at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:23.200
opening ceremony. From the outside, her&nbsp;
participation seems completely harmless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:27.800
or even commendable, as the World Youth&nbsp;
Forum presents itself as a humanitarian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:32.040
group aiming to improve the state of&nbsp;
the world for the younger generations.

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:37.200
The controversy stems from the event's ties&nbsp;
to Egyptian President Abdel Fattah al-Sisi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:42.200
who has been labeled as a dictator by activist&nbsp;
groups in Egypt and elsewhere in the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:46.480
More than 100 individuals, including&nbsp;
many prominent human rights activists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:50.200
signed a joint letter condemning&nbsp;
Hunt's involvement in the event.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.600
The activists called Hunt out directly by saying,

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:58.840
"As you shake hands with Sisi, smile, take&nbsp;
a photo, let history note that you chose to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:04.800
support a dictator responsible for thousands of&nbsp;
deaths, arbitrary detentions, and disappearances."

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:09.040
The arbitrary detentions mentioned in the&nbsp;
letter refer to the wrongful imprisonment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:14.520
of journalists and LGBTQ+ individuals at&nbsp;
the hands of al-Sisi's administration.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.920
It is possible that Hunt signed&nbsp;
up for what she thought was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:20.960
humanitarian event without being aware&nbsp;
of the controversy that would follow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:25.600
but she was certainly made aware of it after&nbsp;
the huge backlash became public. Nevertheless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:30.120
Hunt went ahead and gave her speech&nbsp;
at the World Youth Forum all the same.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:34.680
In the early days of the COVID-19 pandemic,&nbsp;
the film industry shut down completely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:40.640
causing the production of many films to be delayed&nbsp;
as everyone went into lockdown. Slowly but surely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:44.920
projects with contained locations and&nbsp;
limited casts began coming together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:49.440
again until the industry found its footing&nbsp;
once more. One of the first films to come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:54.040
out of the social-distancing era&nbsp;
of the pandemic was How It Ends.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:58.080
The film was written and directed&nbsp;
by Daryl Wein and Zoe Lister-Jones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:02.040
the latter of whom also starred&nbsp;
in the film. As the title implies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:07.120
the film is a comedy about the end of the world,&nbsp;
but rather than fully embracing the medical threat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:12.000
of the COVID-19 pandemic, the virus was&nbsp;
swapped for a meteor headed toward Earth.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:15.080
"Do you actually believe the&nbsp;
news? The meteor is fake."

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:18.240
While most of the small-scale movies&nbsp;
made during this first phase of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:22.520
pandemic kept their casts as tiny&nbsp;
as possible for practical reasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:27.880
How It Ends went in the opposite direction. The&nbsp;
film was packed with a slew of stars including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:33.200
Olivia Wilde, Charlie Day, Bradley&nbsp;
Whitford, Colin Hanks, Fred Armisen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:38.280
Logan Marshall-Green, Whitney Cummings,&nbsp;
Finn Wolfhard, and of course, Helen Hunt.

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:44.120
The film takes place almost entirely outside, with&nbsp;
the cast observing social distancing guidelines.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:49.360
It mostly unfolds like a series of vignettes as&nbsp;
Lister-Jones walks through empty streets during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:54.640
lockdown. It never aimed to be anything more than&nbsp;
a bit of harmless fun during a trying time for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:59.840
the industry, and the film didn't have much of a&nbsp;
shelf life beyond the era in which it was made.

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:05.720
What's more, the film's lackluster legacy was&nbsp;
surely cemented by the release of Don't Look Up, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:11.000
much higher-budget movie with an almost identical&nbsp;
concept that came out the very same year.

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:16.240
1996's Twister was one of the biggest box&nbsp;
office hits of Helen Hunt's career. The film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:20.600
was the second highest-grossing movie of the&nbsp;
year, blowing all of the competition out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:24.480
the water except for Independence&nbsp;
Day. More than two decades later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:29.760
a potential sequel looms on the horizon&nbsp;
— but not the one Hunt would have liked.

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:34.840
After working on the original film in front of the&nbsp;
camera only, Hunt wanted to expand her involvement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:40.640
in the sequel. She wrote a script for Twister&nbsp;
2 alongside her Blindspotting collaborators,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:45.760
Daveed Diggs and Rafael Casal. Hunt also&nbsp;
planned to direct the sequel herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:48.440
but could not find a studio willing to play ball.

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:53.000
Hunt and Diggs both pointed to the script's&nbsp;
emphasis on diversity as the possible reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:57.840
why it was a non-starter for the studio.&nbsp;
Speaking to Insider, Hunt explained,

00:15:57.840 --> 00:16:01.640
"I tried to get it made, with&nbsp;
Daveed and Rafael and me writing it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:05.480
and all Black and Brown storm&nbsp;
chasers, and they wouldn't do it."

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:10.080
Later on in the interview, Diggs elaborated that&nbsp;
a factor for why the movie was never made was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:15.960
for a quote, "shady" reason that he found to be a&nbsp;
typical issue in the contemporary film industry.

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:21.040
A completely different Twister sequel titled&nbsp;
Twisters is currently in the works with an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:25.320
expected release date of summer 2024.&nbsp;
The plot is said to revolve around the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:29.800
daughter of the main characters played&nbsp;
by Hunt and Bill Paxton in the original.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:34.400
The bulk of the cast of Twisters has already&nbsp;
been publicly announced, but Hunt's name is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:39.000
not on the list. While a reason for Hunt's&nbsp;
absence has yet to be publicly announced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:44.160
it's possible she simply wasn't asked to return,&nbsp;
or that she chose not to reprise her role after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:48.880
her own sequel script was rejected. For all we&nbsp;
know, she could even be involved with Twisters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:53.600
in an unexpected way, but her presence is&nbsp;
being kept under wraps for the time being.

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:58.480
Regardless, it seems that Hunt's initial vision&nbsp;
for a Twister sequel will never come to life.

